{"name":"Chinaberry","hex":"#464960","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chinaberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The bead tree or azedarach, Melia azedarach, a deciduous tree in the mahogany family Meliaceae, native to India, southern China and Australia, or its fruit.","The soapberry (genus Sapindus, especially Sapindus saponaria), native to the Americas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chinaberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chinaberry (Aiken, South Carolina)","blocks":[{"text":"Chinaberry, also known as Williams-Converse House, is a house in Aiken, South Carolina that was built in 1824. It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1982."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Chinaberry.jpg/330px-Chinaberry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinaberry_(Aiken%2C_South_Carolina)"},{"title":"Melia azedarach","blocks":[{"text":"Melia azedarach, commonly known as the chinaberry tree, pride of India, bead-tree, Cape lilac, syringa berrytree, Persian lilac, Indian lilac, or white cedar, is a species of deciduous tree in the mahogany family, Meliaceae, that is native to Indomalaya and Australasia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Cinamomo_%28Melia_azedarach%29_em_Bag%C3%A9%2C_RS%2C_Brasil%2C_final_de_outono%2C_frutificado_e_com_folhas_j%C3%A1_ca%C3%ADdas_-_55336704649.jpg/330px-Cinamomo_%28Melia_azedarach%29_em_Bag%C3%A9%2C_RS%2C_Brasil%2C_final_de_outono%2C_frutificado_e_com_folhas_j%C3%A1_ca%C3%ADdas_-_55336704649.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melia_azedarach"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Melia_azedarach_01434.jpg/500px-Melia_azedarach_01434.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://th